    "title": "Item 1A. Risk Factors",
    "start_page": 39
  },
  {
    "title": "Risks related to COVID-19 and other potential pandemics:",
    "start_page": 39
  },
  {
    "title": "We are unable to predict the ultimate impact of the CARES Act and other stimulus and relief legislation or the effect\nthat such legislation and other governmental responses intended to assist providers in responding to COVID-19 may\nhave on our business, financial condition, results of operations or cash flows.",
    "start_page": 40
  },
  {
    "title": "The emergence and effects related to a potential future pandemic, epidemic or outbreak of an infectious disease could\nadversely affect our operations.",
    "start_page": 41
  },
  {
    "title": "Risks related to our indebtedness:",
    "start_page": 41
  },
  {
    "title": "Our debt agreements contain restrictions that limit our flexibility in operating our business.",
    "start_page": 42
  },
  {
    "title": "Risks related to human capital:",
    "start_page": 43
  },
  {
    "title": "We may be unable to attract, hire and retain a highly qualified and diverse workforce, including key management.",
    "start_page": 43
  },
  {
    "title": "Our performance depends on our ability to recruit and retain quality physicians.",
    "start_page": 44
  },
  {
    "title": "Risks related to technology, data privacy and cybersecurity:",
    "start_page": 44
  },
  {
    "title": "Our operations could be impaired by a failure of our information systems.",
    "start_page": 45
  },
  {
    "title": "Health care technology initiatives, particularly those related to sharing patient data and interoperability, may\nadversely affect our operations.",
    "start_page": 46
  },
  {
    "title": "We may not be reimbursed for the cost of expensive, new technology.",
    "start_page": 46
  },
  {
    "title": "Risks related to governmental regulation and other legal matters:",
    "start_page": 46
  },
  {
    "title": "Changes in government health care programs may adversely affect our revenues.",
    "start_page": 47
  },
  {
    "title": "State efforts to regulate the construction or expansion of health care facilities could impair our ability to operate and\nexpand our operations.",
    "start_page": 50
  },
  {
    "title": "We may incur additional tax liabilities.",
    "start_page": 51
  },
  {
    "title": "We have been and could become the subject of government investigations, claims and litigation.",
    "start_page": 51
  },
  {
    "title": "We may be subject to liabilities from claims brought against our facilities, which are costly to defend and may require\nus to pay significant damages if not covered by insurance.",
    "start_page": 51
  },
  {
    "title": "Risks related to operations, strategy, demand and competition:",
    "start_page": 51
  },
  {
    "title": "Our hospitals and other facilities face competition for patients from other hospitals and health care providers.",
    "start_page": 51
  },
  {
    "title": "Any increase in the volume of uninsured patients or deterioration in the collectability of uninsured and patient due\naccounts could adversely affect our results of operations.",
    "start_page": 52
  },
  {
    "title": "If our volume of patients with private health insurance coverage declines or we are unable to retain and negotiate\nfavorable contracts with private third-party payers, including managed care plans, our revenues may be adversely\naffected.",
    "start_page": 53
  },
  {
    "title": "Changes to physician utilization practices and treatment methodologies, third-party payer controls designed to reduce\ninpatientservices orsurgical procedures and otherfactors outside our control that impact demand for medicalservices\nmay reduce our revenues.",
    "start_page": 54
  },
  {
    "title": "We may encounter difficulty acquiring hospitals and other health care businesses, encounter challenges integrating\nthe operations of acquired hospitals and other health care businesses and/or become liable for unknown or contingent\nliabilities as a result of acquisitions.",
    "start_page": 54
  },
  {
    "title": "Our facilities are heavily concentrated in Florida and Texas, which makes us sensitive to regulatory, economic, public\nhealth, environmental and competitive conditions and changes in those states.",
    "start_page": 55
  },
  {
    "title": "Our business and operations are subject to risks related to climate change.",
    "start_page": 55
  },
  {
    "title": "We may be adversely affected if we are not able to achieve our environmental, social and governance (\"ESG\") goals\nor otherwise meet the expectations of our stakeholders with respect to ESG matters.",
    "start_page": 55
  },
  {
    "title": "The industry trend toward value-based purchasing may negatively impact our revenues.",
    "start_page": 56
  },
  {
    "title": "Risks related to macroeconomic conditions:",
    "start_page": 57
  },
  {
    "title": "Our overall business results may suffer during periods of general economic weakness.",
    "start_page": 57
  },
  {
    "title": "We are exposed to market risk related to changes in the market values of securities and interest rates.",
    "start_page": 57
  },
  {
    "title": "Risks related to ownership of our common stock:",
    "start_page": 58
  },
  {
    "title": "There can be no assurance that we will continue to pay dividends.",
    "start_page": 58
  },
  {
    "title": "Certain of our investors may continue to have influence over us.",
    "start_page": 58
  },
